# bromigOS Server (docs/server.md, "The Go Bag"): when a USB drive's filesystem appears, its
# unit starts: bromigos-server-backup-drive@<the filesystem's UUID>.service. The unit asks
# `bromigos-server backup plugged` whether that UUID is the backup drive this server remembers.
# For any other drive it does nothing; for the backup drive, the copy starts.
#
# A device with a USB parent (SUBSYSTEMS: a stick, a disk in a USB enclosure), with a
# filesystem that has a UUID (60-persistent-storage.rules reads both). systemd starts a wanted
# unit once per plugging in, not again when the device changes.
#
# The USB parent is matched on the last line, positively. Negated (SUBSYSTEMS!="usb" with a
# GOTO) it would be true for the first device on the way up that isn't USB, which is the
# block device itself, and every drive would be skipped.
#
# To turn it off: sudo ln -s /dev/null /etc/udev/rules.d/65-bromigos-server-backup-drive.rules
ACTION=="remove", GOTO="bromigos_backup_drive_end"
SUBSYSTEM!="block", GOTO="bromigos_backup_drive_end"
ENV{ID_FS_USAGE}!="filesystem", GOTO="bromigos_backup_drive_end"
ENV{ID_FS_UUID}!="?*", GOTO="bromigos_backup_drive_end"
SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="bromigos-server-backup-drive@$env{ID_FS_UUID}.service"
LABEL="bromigos_backup_drive_end"
